    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46018" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑψι-άομαι</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑψία</span>) 
			Ep.
		 Verb, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>amuse
			oneself</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρῃσι καθήμενοι ἑψιαάσθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.530
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑψιάασθαι μολπῇ καὶ φόρμιγγι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.429
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφ᾽ ἀστραγάλοισι . . ἑψιόωντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.118
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.459
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cer.</u>
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				10.326
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐψιόωντο</span>, as if from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος</span>, Philon. (?) ap.
				Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.118
			</span></i>; but cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφεψιάομαι</span>).</div>
